# Copy to .env.local. Dev uses PGlite (no DATABASE_URL needed).
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET=           # openssl rand -hex 32
BETTER_AUTH_URL=http://localhost:37264
PGLITE_DIR=.pglite
# Prod (Neon) + OAuth — leave unset in dev:
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://...neon...
# GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
# GITHUB_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION. Salts the hash behind the public like cap's visitor key.
# `app/lib/likes-cap.ts` THROWS when this is unset and NODE_ENV=production, rather
# than falling back to its dev default: this repo is public, so the default salt is a
# published one, and `like_grants.visitor_key` would be a reversible IP hash (2^32
# IPv4 enumeration) while the schema comment claims otherwise. Any long random value:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
# LIKES_SALT=

# OPTIONAL. Canonical origin for canonical links, og:image URLs, sitemap.xml and
# robots.txt. `app/lib/site.ts` defaults to https://frames.zentry.com, so set this
# only when serving the explorer somewhere else (a staging domain you actually
# want indexed, a fork). Deliberately NOT derived from BETTER_AUTH_URL — that is
# the auth callback origin, which in dev is localhost, and letting it win here
# would publish localhost canonicals from any build that saw a dev .env.
# Preview deployments need no value: they canonicalise to production on purpose
# and robots.txt disallows them wholesale.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://frames.zentry.com
